From 989727e8406d41006139ad4975069c8fb8d6e67e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: haol666 <haol666@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 17:17:51 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] support h264_vgl passthrough encoder on Windows guests

Offer the h264_vgl encoder (virtio-gpu video protocol passthrough to
the KVM host hardware, project haol666/virgl-video-windows) as a H.264
candidate on Windows.

No GPU vendor detection is required: the existing runtime probe in
available_encoders() attempts a real 720p encode through FFmpeg and
silently drops the candidate whenever the bridge is absent, so bare
metal and non-KVM guests are unaffected. Priority is Good so local
hardware encoders (nvenc/qsv/amf) still win on machines that have them.

RustDesk needs no source change; a Cargo [patch] against this fork is
enough to enable it.
---
 src/ffmpeg_ram/encode.rs | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/ffmpeg_ram/encode.rs b/src/ffmpeg_ram/encode.rs
index f9b8d77..4f17331 100644
--- a/src/ffmpeg_ram/encode.rs
+++ b/src/ffmpeg_ram/encode.rs
@@ -195,6 +195,22 @@ impl Encoder {
                 _nv, amf, _intel
             );
 
+            #[cfg(windows)]
+            {
+                // vgl: H.264 encoding passthrough to the KVM host hardware
+                // (Unraid VCN) via the virtio-gpu video protocol - project
+                // haol666/virgl-video-windows. No vendor detection needed:
+                // the runtime probe below attempts a real 720p encode via
+                // FFmpeg's h264_vgl and silently drops the candidate when
+                // the bridge is absent (bare-metal / non-KVM guests).
+                codecs.push(CodecInfo {
+                    name: "h264_vgl".to_owned(),
+                    format: H264,
+                    priority: Priority::Good as _,
+                    ..Default::default()
+                });
+            }
+
             #[cfg(windows)]
             if _intel && contains(Driver::MFX, H264) {
                 codecs.push(CodecInfo {
